# Just Share Relay Worker – Required Secrets & Configuration
#
# This file documents every value you need to supply.
# It is NOT read by the runtime — it's a reference for you (and CI).
#
# ── Wrangler secrets (set via CLI, stored encrypted in Cloudflare) ────────────
#
#   npx wrangler secret put CF_RELAY_HMAC_SECRET
#       A 32-byte hex string used to sign/verify session tokens on both the
#       Worker and the Android app.
#       Generate one: openssl rand -hex 32
#       This value must also be copied to gradle.properties or local.properties
#       in the Android project as:  CF_RELAY_HMAC_SECRET=<value>
#
# ── wrangler.toml fields to fill in ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   account_id
#       Your Cloudflare Account ID.
#       Find it: https://dash.cloudflare.com → right sidebar.
#
# ── Android BuildConfig fields (gradle.properties / local.properties) ─────────
#
#   CF_RELAY_BASE_URL=wss://relay.justshare.app
#       The WebSocket base URL of your deployed Worker.
#       During development with `wrangler dev`, use: ws://localhost:8787
#
#   CF_RELAY_HMAC_SECRET=<same 32-byte hex as the Wrangler secret>
#       Must match what you set via `wrangler secret put`.
#
#   CF_RELAY_ENABLED=true
#       Feature flag. Set to false to keep using the old TCP relay.
#
# ── Custom Domain (optional but recommended) ──────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. Make sure justshare.app is proxied through Cloudflare (orange cloud).
#   2. In the Workers dashboard, go to your Worker → Settings → Domains & Routes.
#   3. Add a Custom Domain: relay.justshare.app
#   4. Uncomment the [[env.production.routes]] block in wrangler.toml.
